---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ArrowDown, ArrowDownToLine, ArrowUpRight, Clipboard } from '@lucide/astro';
import campaign from '../../../public/campaign/computer-club-20261122/provenance.json';
import proof from '../../../public/prints-desktop/workshop-20261125/proof.json';
import { isPrintsHost, printsOrigin } from '../../lib/prints-site.mjs';

const title = 'Make an image worth sharing';
const description = 'A beginner workshop for making a campaign image. Copy a real App Composer Share prompt, see images made through Oyster and Workers AI, then choose a browser, terminal or MCP workflow.';
const canonical = printsOrigin + '/make';
const product = isPrintsHost(Astro.url);
const home = product ? '/' : '/prints-desktop';
const guide = product ? '/guide' : '/prints-desktop/guide';
const campaignRoot = '/campaign/computer-club-20261122/';
const proofRoot = '/prints-desktop/workshop-20261125/';
const campaignPage = 'https://composer.loftwah.com/share/artwork/composer-club-01-friday-release';
const starter = `Create a 4:5 editorial poster about [your two awkward choices].

Left scene: [one concrete object or action that tells the first story].
Right scene: [one object or action that tells the second story].
Use two contrasting ink colours, one focal point per side, and a simple background.

Typeset “[your headline]” at the top. Set “[short left choice]” and “[short right choice]” in large, high-contrast type. Use only those three lines. Keep all lettering comfortably inside the edges.`;
const mcp = 'return await env.PRINTS.listOutputs({});';
const cli = 'npx @fungi.computer/oyster@0.59.0 try';
const original = campaign.find((item) => item.id === 'composer-club-01-friday-release')!;
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: title,
  description,
  url: canonical,
  mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
  image: new URL(campaignRoot + 'friday-release-og.jpg', canonical).href,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Loftwah', url: 'https://loftwah.com/' },
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} printsProduct={product} shareImage={campaignRoot + 'friday-release-og.jpg'} shareAlt="Pick Your Curse, an App Composer Computer Club campaign poster about demo day and production.">
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <article class="workshop" data-workshop>
    <header class="opening">
      <div class="intro">
        <h1>Make an image worth sharing.</h1>
        <p>Start with one good idea. Turn it into a poster, check it at feed size, and keep the original. Then see how to run the same creative workflow on a stack you control.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="primary" href="#brief">Make your first poster <ArrowDown size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
          <a href="#proof">See the Oyster proof <ArrowDown size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="featured">
        <a href={campaignPage}>
          <img src={campaignRoot + 'friday-release-v1.jpg'} width="1080" height="1350" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Pick Your Curse. Perfect demo, haunted prod? Or perfect prod, nobody knows? A red-lit hallway faces a green exhibition room." />
        </a>
        <figcaption><a href={campaignPage}>Haunted rollout <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a><span>App Composer Share · original AI-generated poster</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <nav class="jump" aria-label="Workshop sections">
      <a href="#brief">Write the brief</a><a href="#run">Make the image</a><a href="#proof">See what ran</a><a href="#stack">Follow the stack</a><a href="#choose">Choose your tool</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="brief" class="chapter" aria-labelledby="brief-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="brief-title">Give the image a job.</h2>
        <p>The Computer Club poster asks people to pick a side. Two scenes create the tension. The headline and two choices have to read before someone scrolls past. The published card adds the approved App Composer mark and URL in the finishing frame.</p>
        <p>Pick your own dilemma. Give each side something you could draw. Keep the palette tight and write the exact words before you touch a model.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>Read the original campaign prompt</summary>
          <p id="campaign-prompt">{original.prompt}</p>
          <button type="button" data-copy-target="campaign-prompt" hidden><Clipboard size={16} aria-hidden="true" /> Copy campaign prompt</button>
          <p class="status" role="status" data-copy-status></p>
          <a href={campaignRoot + 'provenance.json'}>Campaign prompts and hashes <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        </details>
      </div>
      <div class="prompt">
        <label for="poster-brief">Your poster brief</label>
        <textarea id="poster-brief" rows="12" spellcheck="false">{starter}</textarea>
        <div class="actions">
          <button type="button" data-copy-target="poster-brief" hidden><Clipboard size={16} aria-hidden="true" /> Copy prompt</button>
          <a href={campaignRoot + 'computer-club-post-kit.zip'} download><ArrowDownToLine size={16} aria-hidden="true" /> Download the example kit</a>
        </div>
        <p class="status" role="status" data-copy-status></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="run" class="chapter" aria-labelledby="run-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="run-title">Make one good print.</h2>
        <p>Start in the browser. Try the terminal or MCP when repeating the workflow saves you time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <h3>In web Prints</h3>
        <p>Start here if you have access to a funded Fungi Team or an Oyster installation with image generation. Check <a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/quickstart">Fungi Hub availability</a> or explore the account-free terminal trial below.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Prints from your Fungi Team or Oyster desktop. Select a Computer and set a gallery folder such as <code>/media</code>. Your Team or installation needs media access and funding.</li>
          <li>Paste your brief. Pick an image model available on that host, choose a portrait size it supports and review the estimate when offered. Generate one draft.</li>
          <li>Check the spelling, crop and contrast at about 300 pixels wide. Change one thing at a time. If a model struggles with lettering, make the scene without words and add the type in your editor.</li>
          <li>Inspect the image in Prints and keep the original in your gallery. Export a 4:5 portrait for the feed and prepare a separate 1200 × 630 image for link previews. You can use <a href="https://media.loftwah.com/tools/images">Media Studio Image Tools</a> to resize your work. Keep the prompt, model and settings with your project. Share the strongest take and its credit.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>If a preview or save fails, check Activity first. Use the existing attempt’s Retry or Resume to recover retained bytes.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/guides/make-and-save-images">Open the official Prints walkthrough <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a><a href={campaignRoot + 'friday-release-og.jpg'}>See the wide share card <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a></div>
        <details>
          <summary>Try it in a terminal</summary>
          <p>With Node 24.20.0 and Git, open an empty folder and start the local Oyster trial. Use <code>node --version</code> to check your runtime. This version of the Oyster desktop publisher expects that exact Node release. It lets you explore the desktop and Apps without a Cloudflare account. Image inference in Prints needs a deployed host with Workers AI configured.</p>
          <pre><code id="oyster-command">{cli}</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy-target="oyster-command" hidden><Clipboard size={16} aria-hidden="true" /> Copy command</button>
          <p class="status" role="status" data-copy-status></p>
          <p>For a terminal agent, install Shiitake and run <code>fungi</code> in your project folder. Ask it to refine your brief into one concrete scene per side. Fungi Team users can connect their Team tools with <code>fungi login --fungi-mcp &lt;team-endpoint&gt;</code>. A generation needs an approved Prints capability on the selected host.</p>
          <figure class="trial">
            <a class="trial-image" href={proofRoot + 'oyster-local-prints.webp'} aria-label="Open the local Prints screenshot at full size">
              <img src={proofRoot + 'oyster-local-prints.webp'} width="1150" height="760" alt="The empty Prints workspace in the fresh local Oyster trial. A notice says media generation is disabled." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            </a>
            <figcaption>Prints open in our fresh Oyster 0.59.0 trial. The local MCP connection worked and the media-generation permission stayed off.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="actions">
            <a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/oyster-quickstart">Oyster quickstart <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
            <a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/guides/use-the-terminal">Shiitake terminal guide <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Try it with an MCP client</summary>
          <p>MCP lets an agent call an App. Connect an approved client to your Oyster host’s <code>/mcp</code> endpoint and give it access to the intended Prints installation. Use a scoped credential via the client’s secret settings. Open its <code>execute</code> tool and start with a library read. If it returns <code>library_unavailable</code>, select the gallery folder in web Prints first.</p>
          <pre><code id="mcp-read">{mcp}</code></pre>
          <button type="button" data-copy-target="mcp-read" hidden><Clipboard size={16} aria-hidden="true" /> Copy read call</button>
          <p class="status" role="status" data-copy-status></p>
          <p>Ask the client to describe the available <code>generateImage</code> method and model settings before writing. Use an actor and Computer approved for creation. Keep the same request ID and inputs when recovering an ambiguous attempt.</p>
          <a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/guides/call-an-app-from-your-own-server">Oyster MCP setup and examples <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="proof" class="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
      <h2 id="proof-title">Two prints that came back.</h2>
      <p>These studies came from real Oyster MCP calls to Prints using Cloudflare Workers AI. Each receipt records the prompt, model, dimensions and original JPEG hash. The Computer Club poster above is a separate Share campaign example.</p>
      <div class="plates">
        {proof.images.map((entry, index) => (
          <figure>
            <a href={proofRoot + entry.image}>
              <img src={proofRoot + entry.image} width={entry.width} height={entry.height} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt={index === 0 ? 'Oxide-red coastal contours and a compass printed on bone paper.' : 'A brass printing tool and oxide-red ink resting over a paper shoreline study.'} />
            </a>
            <figcaption><strong>{index === 0 ? 'Coastal survey' : 'Shoreline press'}</strong><span>{index === 0 ? 'Lucid Origin' : 'Phoenix 1.0'} · {entry.width} × {entry.height}</span></figcaption>
            <details><summary>Read the prompt</summary><p>{entry.prompt}</p></details>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
      <a class="proof-link" href={proofRoot + 'proof.json'}>Read the generation receipts <ArrowUpRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
    </section>

    <section id="stack" class="chapter" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="stack-title">Follow the job from prompt to file.</h2>
        <p>Here’s the ownership case. You can run the App, let an authorised agent do part of the work and keep the files your workflow creates.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="stack">
        <div><dt><a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/ecosystem">Fungi</a></dt><dd>The ecosystem for Apps, agents and Computers. Shiitake is its terminal agent. A Computer is where your working files live.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/guides/run-your-own-oyster">Oyster</a></dt><dd>The App host. People open Apps in the browser and authorised agents can call them over MCP. You can run the host on your own Cloudflare account and decide who can use it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://docs.fungi.computer/apps/prints">Prints and Darkroom</a></dt><dd>Prints accepts the brief, tracks the result and saves it on your Computer. Darkroom connects supported model providers. Prints Desktop gives you a separate local workspace for comparing and exporting images.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/">Cloudflare</a></dt><dd>Workers hosts your deployed Oyster App infrastructure. Containers run the Computers, and Workers AI can run inference without a GPU on your desk. Your account holds the deployment and usage controls.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://composer.loftwah.com/share">App Composer Share</a></dt><dd>The publishing end. Put the selected image, caption and credit in front of people. Keep the originals and process notes in the project.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section id="choose" class="chapter" aria-labelledby="choose-title">
      <div>
        <h2 id="choose-title">Pick the setup that earns its keep.</h2>
        <p>Oyster and Cloudflare make the strongest case when images are part of an ongoing project with files, a team and repeatable agent work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <dl class="stack compare">
          <div><dt>Oyster with Prints</dt><dd>Choose this for a shared library, App access and an agent path on an account you control. Plan for deployment, model funding and maintenance. Self-hosting the Cloudflare Computer needs Workers Paid. <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/">Check inference pricing</a>.</dd></div>
          <div><dt><a href="https://docs.midjourney.com/hc/en-us/articles/33390732264589-Creating-on-Web">Midjourney</a></dt><dd>Choose its hosted editor for quick visual exploration and built-in reference workflows when you want to start in an image tool.</dd></div>
          <div><dt><a href="https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI">ComfyUI</a></dt><dd>Choose it for node-by-node control, portable graphs and supported local inference with suitable hardware. It gives you an explicit pipeline and more setup choices.</dd></div>
          <div><dt><a href="https://composer.loftwah.com/media-studio">Media Studio</a></dt><dd>Choose it for our existing production workbench, edits, exports and publishing workflows. The Studio and Oyster each keep their own job history.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Start with one poster. Keep the prompt, one approved image and the original file. Then decide whether hosting and automation will save you work on the next ten.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="#brief">Start the poster <ArrowUpRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a><a href={guide}>Try the desktop offline <ArrowUpRight size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a><a href={home}>Prints home</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  for (const button of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-workshop] button[data-copy-target]')) {
    const source = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copyTarget ?? '');
    const status = button.closest('details, .prompt')?.querySelector('[data-copy-status]');
    if (!source || !status || !navigator.clipboard?.writeText) continue;
    button.hidden = false;
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const value = source instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement ? source.value : source.textContent ?? '';
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(value);
        status.textContent = 'Copied.';
      } catch {
        if (source instanceof HTMLTextAreaElement) source.select();
        status.textContent = 'Select the text and copy it from here.';
      }
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .workshop { --paper: #ffdab8; --ink: #241a22; --rule: var(--color-border); }
  .workshop :is(section, a) { scroll-margin-top: 30px; }
  .workshop h2 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem); line-height: 1.07; text-wrap: balance; }
  .workshop h3 { margin: 0 0 9px; }
  .workshop p { margin: 0 0 13px; max-width: 64ch; }
  .workshop a { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .workshop :is(a, button, summary, textarea):focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .opening { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, .85fr); align-items: center; gap: clamp(16px,5vw,65px); padding: clamp(18px,4vw,54px); border-radius: 12px; background: #241a22; color: #fff4e9; }
  .opening h1 { margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: clamp(2.35rem,6vw,5.25rem); line-height: 1.01; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.04em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .opening p { max-width: 37ch; color: #e1c9bc; font-size: clamp(1rem,1.8vw,1.2rem); }
  .opening a { color: #ffdab8; }
  .opening a:focus-visible { outline-color: var(--paper); }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; align-items: center; }
  .actions :is(a,button), .proof-link { min-height: 44px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .actions .primary { padding: 0 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
  .actions .primary:hover { background: #ffbc97; }
  .featured, .plates figure { margin: 0; }
  .featured img, .plates img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 5px; }
  .featured img { max-width: 420px; border: 1px solid #725449; }
  .featured figcaption, .plates figcaption { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: baseline; margin-block: 8px 0; font-size: .85rem; }
  .featured figcaption a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; min-height: 44px; }
  .featured figcaption span { color: #e1c9bc; }
  .jump { display: flex; gap: 2px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: 8px; }
  .jump a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; font-weight: 650; }
  .chapter { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,.76fr) minmax(0,1.24fr); gap: 15px clamp(24px,6vw,90px); margin-block: clamp(35px,7vw,90px); }
  .chapter p, .proof > p { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .prompt { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; padding: clamp(12px,2vw,24px); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .prompt label { display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; font-weight: 700; }
  .prompt textarea, .steps pre { width: 100%; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; color: var(--color-foreground); background: var(--color-background); }
  .prompt textarea { resize: vertical; font: inherit; line-height: 1.45; }
  .steps pre { overflow-x: auto; }
  .workshop button { min-height: 44px; padding: 6px 10px; font-size: .88rem; }
  .workshop button[hidden], .status:empty { display: none; }
  .workshop .status { min-height: 1.3lh; margin: 5px 0 0; font-size: .87rem; }
  .workshop details { margin: 12px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .workshop details summary { min-height: 44px; align-content: center; color: var(--color-foreground); font-weight: 680; cursor: pointer; }
  .workshop details a, .stack a { font-weight: 650; }
  .workshop details a:not(.trial-image) { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; min-height: 44px; }
  .workshop details a svg { flex: none; }
  .steps ol { padding-inline-start: 1.5em; }
  .steps li + li { margin-top: .65em; }
  .proof { border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: clamp(18px,4vw,44px); }
  .plates { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 12px 16px; margin: 17px 0 10px; }
  .plates figcaption span { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .trial { margin: 14px 0; }
  .trial-image { display: block; }
  .trial img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; }
  .trial figcaption { margin-top: 6px; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  .stack { margin: 0; }
  .stack div { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 9px 0 11px; }
  .stack dt { font-weight: 750; }
  .stack dd { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .compare { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  @media(max-width: 760px) {
    .opening,.chapter { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); }
    .opening h1 { max-width: 13ch; }
    .featured img { max-width: 100%; }
    .chapter { gap: 4px; }
  }
  @media(max-width: 490px) {
    .opening { padding: 15px; gap: 12px; }
    .plates { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); }
  }
</style>
